Cactus Code Thorn TestRestrictTags
Author(s)    : Liwei Ji <jiliwei.phys@gmail.com>
Maintainer(s): Liwei Ji <jiliwei.phys@gmail.com>
Licence      : LGPL
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Purpose

Regression test for which groups CarpetX restricts from fine to coarse,
according to their checkpoint and restrict tags, and for the explicit
restriction that a thorn can ask for through the exported RestrictNoPoison.

The driver restricts at one of two points, which the parameter
CarpetX::restrict_during_sync chooses, and the two read a missing restrict
tag differently:
  - restrict_during_sync = no: at the end of a step, a group whose
    restrict tag is "yes"; without the tag, the group takes the value of
    its checkpoint tag.
  - restrict_during_sync = yes: when a SYNC fills a group's ghosts, every
    group it SYNCs except those tagged restrict="no", whatever their
    checkpoint tag (issue #183). The SYNC still fills the ghosts of all of
    them.
The tag governs only restriction that the driver starts on its own: an
explicit RestrictNoPoison restricts exactly the groups it is given,
whatever their tags. AsterX relies on this to restrict its restrict="no"
gauge register.

Two levels, no subcycling. CCTK_INITIAL writes coarse_value (1) on level 0
and fine_value (2) on level 1 into six vertex-centred groups, one per row:

  group        tags                              end of step   SYNC
  untagged     none                              restricted    restricted
  ckpt_no      checkpoint="no"                   kept          restricted
  nr           restrict="no"                     kept          kept
  nr_ckpt_no   checkpoint="no" restrict="no"     kept          kept
  ry_ckpt_no   checkpoint="no" restrict="yes"    restricted    restricted
  nr_explicit  restrict="no", restricted by      restricted    restricted
               TestRestrictTags_RestrictExplicit

At CCTK_POSTINITIAL, TestRestrictTags_RestrictExplicit calls
RestrictNoPoison on nr_explicit, and TestRestrictTags_Sync then
SYNCs all six groups. At CCTK_ANALYSIS, which follows the end-of-step
restriction of the initial data (with restrict_during_sync = no; with
yes the driver skips it), TestRestrictTags_Check aborts the run unless
the coarse interior under level 1 holds fine_value for exactly the groups
in restricted_groups, and coarse_value for every other group. For the
groups not in restricted_groups it also checks the ghosts on both levels,
which CarpetX must mark valid: coarse_value on level 0, and on level 1
coarse_value outside the refined cube (prolongated from level 0) and
fine_value inside it. The parameter fine_box_radius gives the cube; the
check fails unless level 1 covers exactly this cube.

The values are compared exactly. Restriction injects vertex values, and
linear prolongation reproduces the constants exactly.

2. Tests

  test/sync_no.par
      CarpetX::restrict_during_sync = no: the driver restricts only at
      the end of the step, the "end of step" column above. Reintroducing
      a tag check in the restriction operation itself fails this test on
      nr_explicit.
  test/sync_yes.par
      CarpetX::restrict_during_sync = yes: the driver restricts only in
      the CCTK_POSTINITIAL SYNC, the "SYNC" column above. A SYNC that
      restricts the groups tagged restrict="no" (issue #183) fails this
      test on nr and nr_ckpt_no; one that reads the checkpoint tag as at
      the end of a step fails it on ckpt_no.
